# The image needs the app and its lock files, nothing else. `data/` in
# particular must never be baked in: the live database lives on a volume, and
# a copy inside the image would shadow an empty mount and look like the bank.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!trainer/
!web/
!scripts/
!deploy/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
# Both are build output, and the build stage makes its own. Copying the host's
# would put whatever a developer happens to have lying around into the image,
# which is the one thing a pinned dependency is supposed to rule out.
web/vendor/
web-dist/
node_modules/
